This suite tests the behaviour of the interfaces of the Single UNIX
Specification, Version 2 that later editions removed, in the form of the
basic suite: one program per function, which exits with 0 when the
function does what the text of the last edition that had it says.

It is V86BSD's, not os-test's (see ../README.V86BSD).  Each test is marked
with that edition (SUSv2, SUSv3 or SUSv4).  The declarations themselves
are tested by the legacy-include suite.
